<title>UK: HSBC, Barclays off after downgrad.</title>
<headline>HSBC, Barclays off after downgrad.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in HSBC Holdings Plc and Barclays Plc dropped on Monday after analyst David Poutney at Panmure Gordon downgraded his recommendation on both banking stocks to &quot;hold&quot; from &quot;buy&quot;, dealers said.</p>
<p>Poutney also lowered his recommendation on Royal Bank of Scotland Plc to &quot;sell&quot; from &quot;hold&quot;.</p>
</text>
